<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 28 August, from 475 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">475 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,551 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orestes drives Western Emperor Julius Nepos from Ravenna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> seized Ravenna and Julius Nepos fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>. Orestes then made his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> emperor; he would be the last to rule in the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">663 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,363 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tang and Silla forces destroy the Yamato fleet at Baekgang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the mouth of the Geum river in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, Tang and Silla forces fought the fleet of Yamato <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, sent to support the Baekje restoration movement. The Tang navy destroyed the Japanese fleet, ending hopes of reviving Baekje.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baekgang">Battle of Baekgang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1189">1189 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">837 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Guy of Lusignan begins the siege of Acre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, began the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, his first significant counterattack against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> and part of what became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>. The siege lasted until July 1191 and ended in a key crusader victory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1290">1290 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">736 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Birgham is ratified at Northampton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The second Treaty of Birgham, under which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-maid-of-norway">Margaret, Maid of Norway</a>, was to marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england">Edward of Caernarfon</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a>, was ratified at Northampton. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> was to remain separate from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, but Margaret died on her voyage to Scotland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-maid-of-norway">Margaret, Maid of Norway</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england">Edward II of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1565">1565 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">461 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro Menéndez sights Florida and names it for St Augustine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</a> sighted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> coast on the feast of St Augustine and gave the saint's name to the harbour. He founded the settlement on 8 September; it is the oldest continuously occupied European city in the US.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First issue of Scientific American is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Inventor Rufus Porter launched Scientific American as a weekly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. It is the oldest continuously published monthly magazine in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther King gives his 'I Have a Dream' speech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking to some 250,000 people at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-on-washington">March on Washington</a>, King described his dream of a nation free from racial injustice. The march helped build support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-rights-act-of-1964">Civil Rights Act of 1964</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2005">2005 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Orleans orders its first mandatory evacuation as Katrina nears</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With Hurricane Katrina at Category 5 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>, Mayor Ray Nagin ordered the city's first-ever mandatory evacuation. Tens of thousands without transport sheltered in the Superdome.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 28 August <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elisabeth-christine-of-brunswick-wolfenbuttel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elisabeth-christine-of-brunswick-wolfenbuttel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elisabeth Christine of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</span><span class="tp">1691–1750</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Wolfgang von Goethe</span><span class="tp">1749–1832</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-duke-of-teck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-duke-of-teck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis, Duke of Teck</span><span class="tp">1837–1900</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-fraser"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-fraser.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter Fraser</span><span class="tp">1884–1950</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 28 August <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/magnus-maximus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/magnus-maximus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Magnus Maximus</span><span class="tp">c. 335–388</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/augustine-of-hippo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augustine-of-hippo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Augustine of Hippo</span><span class="tp">354–430</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinich-janaab-pakal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">K'inich Janaab Pakal</span><span class="tp">603–683</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xingzong-of-liao"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Xingzong of Liao</span><span class="tp">1016–1055</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muin-al-din-unur"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mu'in al-Din Unur</span><span class="tp">d. 1149</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-berkeley-1st-baron-berkeley-of-stratton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-berkeley-1st-baron-berkeley-of-stratton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Berkeley, 1st Baron Berkeley of Stratton</span><span class="tp">1602–1678</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/junipero-serra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/junipero-serra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Junípero Serra</span><span class="tp">1713–1784</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adam-philippe-comte-de-custine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adam-philippe-comte-de-custine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adam Philippe, Comte de Custine</span><span class="tp">1740–1793</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boris-iii-of-bulgaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boris-iii-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Boris III of Bulgaria</span><span class="tp">1894–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-naguib"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muhammad-naguib.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Muhammad Naguib</span><span class="tp">1901–1984</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
